# Downloaded benchmark data. Roughly 1.4 GB across the corpora, all of it
# re-fetchable: benchmarks/fetch_socrata100.py, fetch_corpus.py, fetch_matrix.py
# and make_hostile.py rebuild every one of these from public sources. What is
# committed instead is the *manifest* -- benchmarks/socrata100-manifest.json --
# which pins exactly which datasets were used and why each rejection was
# rejected. The data is reproducible; the selection is the thing that has to be
# on the record.
corpus/
corpus100/
corpus500/
corpus_matrix/
corpus_hostile/

# Sweep working files. The JSONL, the summary and the CSV under results/ are
# committed on purpose -- they are the evidence -- but the truncated copies and
# the progress logs are not.
results/truncated/
results/*.log
benchmarks/*-fetch.log
benchmarks/*-gen.log
benchmarks/cross-column.log
benchmarks/overnight.log
